A block box's own percentage min/max widths resolved against a zero base inside its shrink-to-fit width, so
max-width: 100% clamped the measured content to nothing. They are cyclic there and now behave as zero and none
(CSS Sizing 3 5.2.1). A column flex item's hypothetical cross size clamps by its min/max widths, which resolve
against the flex container, as a fit-content width does.

